1 as writable primary and node2/node3 as read-only standbys\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node1 initialized with wal_level=replica, hot_standby, max_wal_senders/replication_slots, and pg_hba rules for the replicator role and subnet. Both node2 and node3 were built via pg_basebackup -R against node1 into physical replication slots and started. pg_is_in_recovery() returns false on node1 and true on node2/node3 (cmd-11fabaa007aa49c8, cmd-b5df33a0df444ba1), and pg_stat_replication on node1 shows both standbys in 'streaming' state (cmd-8338e5ad1e0a4345).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-2fb39997ba114e2b\",\"cmd-6249e9e364ea4719\",\"cmd-3b70c5fdc20f4c01\",\"cmd-07f3084a41cf4a82\",\"cmd-37ff7c0108a04ee2\",\"cmd-7e1ecc6f2dbd49fa\",\"cmd-51f31241b79c4f28\",\"cmd-5225ab506c9d4758\",\"cmd-11fabaa007aa49c8\",\"cmd-b5df33a0df444ba1\",\"cmd-8338e5ad1e0a4345\"]},{\"id\":\"replication-visibility\",\"requirement\":\"Changes committed on the primary should be visible on both standbys\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A table repl_test was created and a row inserted on node1; the row was directly observed via SELECT on both node2 and node3 (cmd-c8089c9922534ecf, cmd-3bbb94bb58d34e32). Both standbys also rejected an attempted CREATE TABLE with 'cannot execute ... in a read-only transaction', confirming they are read-only.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-33a48cc251964a9e\",\"cmd-c8089c9922534ecf\",\"cmd-3bbb94bb58d34e32\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node2\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol on node2: healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered service/data/cluster state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline captured boot_id 95e2f83d... with postgresql-15 active/in-recovery and repl_test count=1 (cmd-10aa5c41a7a04564). systemctl reboot was issued and acknowledged (cmd-0537302ceaec4a54); node was unreachable during the transition (cmd-e7566dbdc76b4041, cmd-745976c742e54b41) then returned a new boot_id 73c42012... (cmd-99d23e8dcf3e4e8f). Post-restart, postgresql-15 is active/in-recovery with repl_test count=1 intact (cmd-ccc7550cc2874559), and node1's pg_stat_replication shows node2 streaming again (cmd-81b1c1812559413e). This matches the fixed global before/after-executor boot-identity snapshots.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-10aa5c41a7a04564\",\"cmd-0537302ceaec4a54\",\"cmd-e7566dbdc76b4041\",\"cmd-745976c742e54b41\",\"cmd-99d23e8dcf3e4e8f\",\"cmd-ccc7550cc2874559\",\"cmd-81b1c1812559413e\",\"global:before_prepare:node2:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node3\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol on node3: healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered service/data/cluster state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline captured boot_id 9294b73f... with postgresql-15 active/in-recovery and repl_test count=1 (cmd-b9b166224d604fbe). systemctl reboot was issued and acknowledged (cmd-11b38b528d09475b); node was unreachable during the transition (cmd-0f7320edf083401e, cmd-b2cb771db45f44bf) then returned a new boot_id 218e1f5d... (cmd-ea3e049a209040a8). Post-restart, postgresql-15 is active/in-recovery with repl_test count=1 intact (cmd-6003af0f50b441b6), and node1's pg_stat_replication shows node3 streaming again (cmd-a88968d9569f453d). This matches the fixed global before/after-executor boot-identity snapshots.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-b9b166224d604fbe\",\"cmd-11b38b528d09475b\",\"cmd-0f7320edf083401e\",\"cmd-b2cb771db45f44bf\",\"cmd-ea3e049a209040a8\",\"cmd-6003af0f50b441b6\",\"cmd-a88968d9569f453d\",\"global:before_prepare:node3:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node1\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol on node1 (primary): healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered service/data/cluster state including resumed replication\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline captured boot_id 33b0e84c... with postgresql-15 active/not-in-recovery, both standbys already streaming (cmd-740dec7f60b24f10, cmd-9a681dfe8f5a4471). systemctl reboot was issued and acknowledged (cmd-f45cf9f498734c86), with the node unreachable during the transition (cmd-ade5d5ce97824ef4, cmd-33954f4c52c140cc) before returning a new boot_id f44af3d4... (cmd-81ab0ec951254d22). Post-restart, postgresql-15 is active/not-in-recovery; a new row was inserted (count=2 in repl_test) and this was directly confirmed as replicated to both node2 and node3 (cmd-dad0a414de5d405f, cmd-4b99aafb98cc46a2), and pg_stat_replication on node1 shows both standbys streaming again (cmd-536cbd84fe0442d8). Standby logs corroborate the primary going down and streaming resuming (cmd-dad0a414de5d405f).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-740dec7f60b24f10\",\"cmd-9a681dfe8f5a4471\",\"cmd-f45cf9f498734c86\",\"cmd-ade5d5ce97824ef4\",\"cmd-33954f4c52c140cc\",\"cmd-81ab0ec951254d22\",\"cmd-33d250ae4105495d\",\"cmd-dad0a414de5d405f\",\"cmd-4b99aafb98cc46a2\",\"cmd-536cbd84fe0442d8\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.75,\"summary\":\"Most state-changing commands map clearly to task needs: killing a pre-existing stuck 'yum -q check' process that held the yum lock on all three nodes was a necessary unblocking action (cmd-263e482f524447b8, cmd-6bcd1c37eed94c42, cmd-791f059bf21c42d3), and the subsequent rpm --rebuilddb on node3 (cmd-1a3adf83944a4d39) was a direct, bounded corrective action for rpmdb corruption caused by that kill — not an unrelated experiment. Config edits, replication slot creation, pg_basebackup, and firewalld opening of the postgresql service on all three nodes are all directly tied to the replication requirement and were retained appropriately. The replicator password and cluster SSH private key used to relay it were shredded/removed after use on all three nodes (cmd-59ac4744140d4be8, cmd-33b7e9bcff2b4a43, cmd-c8f61562501a4f4f), which is 