aptured boot_id 9294b73f... with postgresql-15 active/in-recovery and repl_test count=1 (cmd-b9b166224d604fbe). systemctl reboot was issued and acknowledged (cmd-11b38b528d09475b); node was unreachable during the transition (cmd-0f7320edf083401e, cmd-b2cb771db45f44bf) then returned a new boot_id 218e1f5d... (cmd-ea3e049a209040a8). Post-restart, postgresql-15 is active/in-recovery with repl_test count=1 intact (cmd-6003af0f50b441b6), and node1's pg_stat_replication shows node3 streaming again (cmd-a88968d9569f453d). This matches the fixed global before/after-executor boot-identity snapshots.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b9b166224d604fbe","cmd-11b38b528d09475b","cmd-0f7320edf083401e","cmd-b2cb771db45f44bf","cmd-ea3e049a209040a8","cmd-6003af0f50b441b6","cmd-a88968d9569f453d","global:before_prepare:node3:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity"]},{"id":"restart-node1","requirement":"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol on node1 (primary): healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered service/data/cluster state including resumed replication","status":"satisfied","summary":"Baseline captured boot_id 33b0e84c... with postgresql-15 active/not-in-recovery, both standbys already streaming (cmd-740dec7f60b24f10, cmd-9a681dfe8f5a4471). systemctl reboot was issued and acknowledged (cmd-f45cf9f498734c86), with the node unreachable during the transition (cmd-ade5d5ce97824ef4, cmd-33954f4c52c140cc) before returning a new boot_id f44af3d4... (cmd-81ab0ec951254d22). Post-restart, postgresql-15 is active/not-in-recovery; a new row was inserted (count=2 in repl_test) and this was directly confirmed as replicated to both node2 and node3 (cmd-dad0a414de5d405f, cmd-4b99aafb98cc46a2), and pg_stat_replication on node1 shows both standbys streaming again (cmd-536cbd84fe0442d8). Standby logs corroborate the primary going down and streaming resuming (cmd-dad0a414de5d405f).","evidence_ids":["cmd-740dec7f60b24f10","cmd-9a681dfe8f5a4471","cmd-f45cf9f498734c86","cmd-ade5d5ce97824ef4","cmd-33954f4c52c140cc","cmd-81ab0ec951254d22","cmd-33d250ae4105495d","cmd-dad0a414de5d405f","cmd-4b99aafb98cc46a2","cmd-536cbd84fe0442d8","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.9,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.75,"summary":"Most state-changing commands map clearly to task needs: killing a pre-existing stuck 'yum -q check' process that held the yum lock on all three nodes was a necessary unblocking action (cmd-263e482f524447b8, cmd-6bcd1c37eed94c42, cmd-791f059bf21c42d3), and the subsequent rpm --rebuilddb on node3 (cmd-1a3adf83944a4d39) was a direct, bounded corrective action for rpmdb corruption caused by that kill — not an unrelated experiment. Config edits, replication slot creation, pg_basebackup, and firewalld opening of the postgresql service on all three nodes are all directly tied to the replication requirement and were retained appropriately. The replicator password and cluster SSH private key used to relay it were shredded/removed after use on all three nodes (cmd-59ac4744140d4be8, cmd-33b7e9bcff2b4a43, cmd-c8f61562501a4f4f), which is good practice. Two residual issues remain and were not cleaned up: (1) installation/reboot log files and pid files (/tmp/pgdg_install.log, /tmp/pg_install.log, /tmp/pgdg.pid, /tmp/reboot.log, and on node1 /tmp/pkgs.html) were left on all three nodes per the after-executor snapshot, representing minor abandoned residue with no functional impact; (2) the cluster SSH public key that was appended to each node's own authorized_keys (cmd-18427e52cfcc412b, cmd-efb70442c79f406b, cmd-06ea2d6fe6764631) to enable the password relay was never removed, though its paired private key was shredded, so it should be inert but is nonetheless an un-reverted grant. Both are bounded, low-risk, and do not affect the core replication outcome.","evidence_ids":["cmd-263e482f524447b8","cmd-6bcd1c37eed94c42","cmd-791f059bf21c42d3","cmd-1a3adf83944a4d39","cmd-18427e52cfcc412b","cmd-efb70442c79f406b","cmd-06ea2d6fe6764631","cmd-59ac4744140d4be8","cmd-33b7e9bcff2b4a43","cmd-c8f61562501a4f4f","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"The executor successfully configured PostgreSQL 15 streaming replication with node1 as a writable primary and node2/node3 as read-only async standbys, and directly demonstrated that writes on the primary replicate to both standbys while standbys reject writes. The mandatory node-restart evidence protocol was executed sequentially (node2, node3, node1) with pre-restart baselines, acknowledged systemctl reboot commands, changed boot identities corroborated by the fixed lifecycle snapshots, and confirmed post-restart recovery of the PostgreSQL service, intact replicated data, and resumed streaming in both directions (including the primary re-accepting writes and both standbys reconnecting). Operational hygiene is good overall; environment obstacles (stale yum lock, corrupted rpmdb, dead PGDG12-14 mirrors, missing libicu/libzstd) were handled with bounded corrective actions, though a few installation log/pid files and an SSH authorized_keys entry were left behind without cleanup.","limitations":["Native package-manager consistency checks (package-health) were unavailable/timed out at every lifecycle phase on all three nodes, so package-level integrity cannot be independently verified beyond the observed yum/rpm command output.","Leftover installation and reboot log files (/tmp/pgdg_install.log, /tmp/pg_install.log, /tmp/pgdg.pid, /tmp/reboot.log, /tmp/pkgs.html) remain on the nodes per the after-executor snapshot; these appear to be inert diagnostic residue rather than functional issues.","The cluster SSH public key added to each node's own authorized_keys during password relay was not removed, though the corresponding private key was shredded on all nodes, limiting practical exposure."]},"ttft_ms":27325,"type":"result","duration_ms":101754,"uuid":"57ddb7af-0c4b-45a9-bac7-58dbe28cac78","ttft_stream_ms":1241,"time_to_request_ms":43,"first_content_frame_ms":1554,"queued_turn_count":0}
